# Practical Example

Consider a product card:

```html
<div class="card">

    <h2>Wireless Headphones</h2>

    <p>₹1,999</p>

    <button class="delete">
        Delete
    </button>

</div>
```

JavaScript:

```javascript
const button = document.querySelector(".delete");

button.addEventListener("click", function() {

    const card = button.closest(".card");

    const title = card.firstElementChild;

    console.log("Deleting:", title.textContent);

    card.remove();

});
```

Here we use multiple DOM concepts:

```text
button
   ↓
closest(".card")
   ↓
firstElementChild
   ↓
textContent
   ↓
remove()
```

